 @MicroTypeEngineering  Im currently dealing with a circuit where a 800ma Voltage Regulator located near the 12-18v DC power input is getting hot to the touch. The component in question is MC33269 in the 269AJC DPAK DT suffix

This could for a myriad of reasons but I suspect possibly injecting +42v into the circuit could have destroyed one of the components. 

Thankyou for your response!

I saw your post in the link you have mentioned. I would like to make a small question regarding the current you have calculated in that blog.  For the current calculation you have used the driver voltage divided by the resistance. But i have found something different which is  gate current is equal to the Voltage difference between the driver and the gate(which separated by resistor) divided by the resistance. As found in this link;

https://www.vishay.com/docs/73217/an608a.pdf

Can you please update us about this?
